# Client Order Place speed (busy dinner)

## Feel targets
| Action | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Button first response | Instant (&lt;50ms visual) |
| Add item | &lt;150ms on screen |
| Open table → order | &lt;300ms feel |
| Category switch | &lt;100ms |
| Send to kitchen | UI instant; Mother can finish after |
| Open Restaurant | Tables visible immediately from cache |
| Sync / Update All | Till stays usable |

## Architecture
- Client → Mother HTTP for order mutations (no Client→cloud).
- Optimistic UI + warm SQLite cache; sync in background.
- First tap must always work — no invisible dismiss layers after close.

## Phase 1 (Order Place) — done
Optimistic add · Incremental shell · Warm menu · Instant Send/Pay · Serial Mother persist

## Phase 2 (Floor / Live / Sync) — done
Restaurant cache-first · Table→Order Place · Update All non-blocking · Live debounce · Login warm-cache

## Phase 3 (First tap) — done
1. Pos sidebar: `InputTransparent` + remove overlay on select; navigate immediately; short parallel close.
2. SharedUI `ApplicationShellFrame`: nav/dialog/error/toast layers drop hit-testing when closed.
3. Guest overlays, virtual keyboard, reservation dialog: dismiss sets `InputTransparent` then removes from tree.

## Phase 4 (Smooth under load) — done
1. Shared header clock (`ApplicationHeader`); legacy MainPage clock only while those labels exist.
2. Idle logout stays 3 min via one-shot timer (no 1 Hz work).
3. Live/Restaurant WS debounce ~400ms; refresh in place / dirty-skip when unchanged.
4. ChefLoader animates only when revealed; stop timer on hide; no tap-block at opacity 0; shell delay ~280ms.
5. `RestaurantTablesView` syncs status/color/text/position in place (no full card rebuild each refresh).

## Scope
- Default: `OrderWeb.Client` + SharedUI shell/Order Place.
- Do not port Mother AppShell nav-lock / Rider / Visual Table admin.
